.TH "tum\-status" "1" "" "" "tmux\-borrow Manual"
.SS NAME
\f[B]tum\-status\f[R] \[em] emit status\-bar / prompt glyphs for a pane
.SS SYNOPSIS
\f[B]tum status\f[R] [\f[I]pane_id\f[R]]
.PP
\f[B]tum prompt\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]tum status\f[R] \f[B]\-h\f[R] | \f[B]\[en]help\f[R]
.SS DESCRIPTION
\f[B]tum status\f[R] emits the glyph string for a pane, for use in the
tmux status bar (tmux interpolates \f[CR]#{pane_id}\f[R] into
\f[CR]#(tum status #{pane_id})\f[R]).
A host pane with borrowed things attached shows the host glyph (default
\f[CR]÷\f[R], configurable via \f[CR]\[at]tum\-host\-glyph\f[R]); a
borrowed pane shows the borrowed glyph (default \f[CR]§\f[R], via
\f[CR]\[at]tum\-borrowed\-glyph\f[R]) plus the utility name; an orphan
shows a \f[CR]!\f[R] prefix.
.PP
\f[B]tum prompt\f[R] emits the same glyphs as a snippet for the shell
prompt (PS1).
Source it from your \f[CR].bashrc\f[R] (a small snippet ships for that);
optional one\-block snippets for starship and powerlevel10k are
documented but never auto\-patched into your prompt config.
.PP
Both glyphs are configurable through the \f[CR]\[at]tum\-*\f[R] static
options; see \f[B]tum\-defs\f[R](5).
.SS OPTIONS
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\-h\f[R], \f[B]\[en]help\f[R] Print a short synopsis (the SYNOPSIS
and EXAMPLES sections of this page) and exit.
For bare \f[B]tum\f[R], list every subcommand.
.SS EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
# in tmux.conf:  set \-g status\-right \[aq]#(tum status #{pane_id})\[aq]
tum prompt               # PS1 snippet for the shell prompt
# bound to  t g s  in the shipped tum\-bindings.conf
.EE
.SS SEE ALSO
\f[B]tum\-ls\f[R](1), \f[B]tum\-check\f[R](1), \f[B]tum\-defs\f[R](5),
\f[B]tmux\f[R](1)
